// @test: An unresolvable enum payload is a hard error, not a degraded run (#251)
// @description: a payload type that never resolves — a struct that contains the very enum
//   declaring it — has no computable layout. The module still verifies at the LLVM level,
//   so the compiler must refuse to run or link it instead of executing with the payload
//   silently degraded to i64.
// @category: enums, payload, error-handling, regression
// @expect: fail
// @expect-error: Could not resolve payload type for variant

struct S { e<E> }
enum E { V(S) }

main()<Int> -> { return 0 }
